! mcp_bootstrap_p367.strap -- MCP printed page 367: the SYSTEM COMMAND
! package's EOJ command sub-package (J EOJ .. Z EOJ99) and its ABEOJ
! command (Z ABEND .. Z ABJ99), lines 1-52.
!
! docs/MCP_Mar63_250-445.pdf PDF p.117, read at 400 dpi.  Header, READ:
! "TIME CLOCK 00054041  PUNID 22SCOMD  CARD ID WA000290  DIST. OF 3/01
!  3/01  PAGE NUMBER 367"; the heading row's LOCATION field is BLANK.
!
! THE PAGE.  52 lines, every line number prints a "*"; a "*" after the
! LOCATION on lines 12, 26 and 47.  Still PUNID 22SCOMD, card series WA,
! no SLC, no TAIL.  Contiguous 234722.00 .. 234765.40 (line 52's DD
! ends at 234766.00, ZREWCD's printed address on p.361).
!   lines  1-3   remark cards (banner on 2).
!   lines  4-24  J EOJ: SX,JXMSK,$R; CT tests of the command source/mode
!                word; J EOJX; Z EOJX's SIC/BD to Z SPLPR and S PRIME
!                with in-line parameter words (lines 17-18, 21).
!   lines 25-26  CNOP; Z EOJ99 (A*)DD(BU), 32 characters 234740.00 ->
!                234744.00 (the "*" terminator measured at column 32
!                after the comma: 27 printed characters + 5 blanks).
!   lines 27-30  remark cards (banner on 29).
!   lines 31-50  Z ABEND: the same shape (Z AEOJX, Z AEOJZ).
!   lines 51-52  CNOP; Z ABJ99 (A*)DD(BU), 40 characters (36 printed + 4
!                blanks, "*" at column 40) 234761.00 -> 234766.00.
! JOIN.  p.361's JTABL prints B,JEOJ = 234722.10 and B,ZABEND =
! 234744.10: lines 4 and 31 sit exactly there.  p.366 should end at
! 234722.00 (p.361 JEOF 234700.40 .. ); p.368 should open at 234766.00
! (Z REW CD, p.361 B,ZREWCD 234766.10).  No SLC: the deck states the
! origin hard.
!
! GLYPHS SETTLED BY OTHER THAN PLAIN INK:
!   * the drum prints O open throughout: "J ECJ", "JECJX", "Z ECJX",
!     "Z ECJ 99", "Z ECJ99", "ZAECJX", "Z AECJZ", ",DECJ", ",DABECJ",
!     "YECJS", "J NCPX"/"JNCPX", "JCP", "JCV", "JCN" written with O
!     (JEOJ is p.361's spelling; DEOJ/DABEOJ/YEOJS landed; JNOPX is
!     C22-6728's; the J-bits JOP/JOV/JON print the same open round as
!     in p.366/p.368's sheet reads).
!   * "CTIC010"/"CTI0010": the connective 0010 (digits; binary agrees).
!   * line 11 "B,Z ER EX2" = ZEREX2 (blank in a name; line 12 prints it).
!   * line 18 ",4.C" and line 45 ",5.C" = 4.0, 5.0 (open 0; binary
!     000004.00, 000005.00).
!   * hex "C0"/"CO" bytes (lines 11, 38) = 00 (lesson 6).
!
! EXTERNALS (all SCOMD-local ones are not landed; values from this
! page's binary or the neighbours' printed binaries):
!   JXMSK: SX's J field prints .33 = 2J+1, J = 13 -> SYN,$13 (index).
!   JOP=2 (this page, line 5 000002.00); JSR=4 (p.364 line 5 CTI,JSR
!   prints 000004.00); JJ4=16 (p.366 line 5 JSR+JJ4 = 000024.00);
!   JOV=32 (JSR+JJ4+JOV = 000064.00); JJ1=8 (p.366 line 9 JSR+JJ1+JOV =
!   000054.00); JON=128 (JSR+JJ1+JOV+JON = 000254.00).  Each value is
!   pinned by a printed single-symbol or one-new-symbol sum; NONE is
!   from a defining card.  Plain integer SYN, no dds.
!
! CARD SERIALS.  WA000290 .. WA000339: lines 42 and 43 BOTH print
! WA000331, lines 46 and 47 BOTH print WA000334.  Recorded.

